{"id":"word:hebrew:H1350","type":"word","title":"גָּאַל","subtitle":"H1350 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to redeem (according to the Oriental law of kinship), i.e. to be the next of kin (and as such to buy back a relative's property, marry his widow, etc.)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to גָּאַל (H1350) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 105 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"גָּאַל (gâʼal) means to redeem (according to the Oriental law of kinship), i.e. to be the next of kin (and as such to buy back a relative's property, marry his widow, etc.) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 16 11."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"גָּאַל","transliteration":"gâʼal","pronunciation":"gaw-al'","strong":"H1350","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1350","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["גֹּאֵ֣ל","גֹּאֵ֤ל","וְ/גֹאֲלֵ֖/ךְ","יִגְאַל֙","יִגָּאֵ֖ל"],"morphs":[["HVqrmsc",12],["HVqi3ms",8],["HVqrmsa",7],["HVNi3ms",6],["HTd/Vqrmsa",5],["HVqp2ms",4],["HC/Vqrmsc/Sp2fs",4],["HR/Vqc",4],["HVqp3ms",3],["HVqrmsc/Sp3mp",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to redeem (according to the Oriental law of kinship), i.e. to be the next of kin (and as such to buy back a relative's property, marry his widow, etc.)","usage":"× in any wise, × at all, avenger, deliver, (do, perform the part of near, next) kinsfolk(-man), purchase, ransom, redeem(-er), revenger.","full":"H1350. gaal I. גָּאַל verb redeem, act as kinsman (Late Hebrew, Niph`al be redeemed ; also גְּאוּלָּה גּוֺאֵל, ) — Qal Perfect ׳ג , etc. Isa 44:23 14 t.; Imperfect יִגְאַל , etc. Lev 25:33 18 t.; Imperative גְּאַל , etc. Ruth 4:6 3 t.; Infinitive absolute גָּאֹל Lev 27:13 2 t.; construct לִגְאוֺל Ruth 4:4 2 t.; suffix לְגָאֳלֵךְ 3:13 ; Participle גֹּאֵל Lev 25:26 24 t., גּוֺאֵל Isa 59:20 ; Psa 103:4 ; suffix גֹּאַלְךָ Isa 48:17 , גֹּאֲלֵךְ 54:8 (suffix 19 t.); passive plural גְּאוּלִים , etc. 35:9 4 t.; — 1 act as kinsman, do the part of next of kin (chiefly in D H P Ruth), גֹּאֵל kinsman Lev 25:25 (H) Num 5:8 ; 35:12 (P) Ruth 2:20 ; 3:9 , 12 ; 4:1 , 3 , 6 , 8 , 14 ; 1Kin 16:11 . a. in taking a kinsman's widow וגאלתיך לגאלך יחפץ לא ואם יגאל טוב יגאלך אם if he will do thee the kinsman's part (raise up children by the widow) well, let him do the kinsman's part; but if he is not pleased to do thee the kinsman's part then I will do thee the kinsman's part Ruth 3:13 ; b. in redeeming from bondage Lev 25:48-49 , (H); c. in redeeming a field Lev 25:26 , 33 (H) Ruth 4:4 , 6 ; d. claim as kinsman Job 3:5 ; e. הַדָּם גֹּאֵל the avenger of blood Num 35:19 , 21 , 24 , 25 , 27 (twice in verse); Josh 20:3 , 5 (?; not in ᵐ5 ) 20:9 (P). Deut 19:6 , 12 (D) 2Sam 14:11 . 2 redeem , by payment of value assessed, of consecrated things, by the original owner Lev 27:13 , 15 , 19 , 20 , 31 (P). 3 redeem , with God as subject implying personal relationship, chiefly in poetry: — a. individuals , from death Psa 103:4 ; Lam 3:58 ; Hosea 13:14 , רע מכל Gen 48:16 (E poetry), נפשׁ Psa 69:19 ; 72:14 , orphans Prov 23:11 ; Jer 50:34 , וגאלני ריבי ריבה Psa 119:154 , גֹּאֲלִי Job 19:25 , וְגֹאֲלִי צוּרִי Psalm 19:15. b. Israel, from Egyptian bondage Exod 6:6 (P?) 15:13 (song) Psa 74:2 ; 77:16 ; 78:35 , אויב מיד 106:10 . c. from exile (chiefly Isa 3 , the verb not in Isa 1 ) Isa 43:1 ; 44:22-23 , 48:20 ; 52:9 ; 63:9 ; Micah 4:10 , מיד Psa 107:2 ; Jer 31:11 ; Yahweh is גֹּאֵל Isa 41:14 ; 43:14 ; 44:6 , 24 ; 47:4 ; 48:17 ; 49:7 , 26 ; 54:5 , 8 ; 59:20 ; 60:16 ; 63:16 ; and the people גְּאוּלִים 35:9 ; 51:10 ; 62:12 ; 63:4 (compare גְּאוּלַי below), Psa 107:2 . Niph`al Perfect נִגְאָ֑ל Lev 25:49 ; Imperfect יִגָּאֵל 25:30 5 t.; תִּגָּאֵ֑לוּ Isa 52:3 ; &#8212; 1 reflexive redeem oneself Lev 25:49 (H). 2 pass . be redeemed , a. field Lev 25:30 (H), slave 25:54 (H); b. consecrated things Lev 27:20 , 27 , 28 , 33 (P); c. Jerusalem by Yahweh Isa 52:3 . גְּאוּלַי Isa 63:4 , in ג ׳שְׁנַת , noun abstract redemption , according to ᵑ9 ᵑ6 ᵐ5 Ges Hi De MV Che Di RVm; then either plural abstract suffix year of ( my ) redemption (so most); or abstract form. in י֯ , after Syriac analogy, Lag Symm. ii. 101 f. Semitic i. 19, 68. BN 192 ( ᵐ5 omit my ); but &lt; Passive participle plural suffix my ransomed ( released ) ones Ew Br Brd AV RV compare below גאל above.","rootNote":"a primitive root,","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 16 11","keyReferences":["1Kgs 16 11","2Sam 14 11","Deut 19 6","Deut 19 12","Exod 6 6","Exod 15 13","Gen 48 16","Hos 13 14"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":105,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 16 11","book":"1Kgs","chapter":16,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/גֹאֲלָ֖י/ו","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqrmpc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"2Sam 14 11","book":"2Sam","chapter":14,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גֹּאֵ֤ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqrmsc"},{"reference":"Deut 19 6","book":"Deut","chapter":19,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גֹּאֵ֨ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqrmsc"},{"reference":"Deut 19 12","book":"Deut","chapter":19,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גֹּאֵ֥ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqrmsc"},{"reference":"Exod 6 6","book":"Exod","chapter":6,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/גָאַלְתִּ֤י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqq1cs"},{"reference":"Exod 15 13","book":"Exod","chapter":15,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גָּאָ֑לְתָּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp2ms"},{"reference":"Gen 48 16","book":"Gen","chapter":48,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/גֹּאֵ֨ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Vqrmsa"},{"reference":"Hos 13 14","book":"Hos","chapter":13,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֶגְאָלֵ֑/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi1cs/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"Isa 35 9","book":"Isa","chapter":35,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"גְּאוּלִֽים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqsmpa"},{"